#: ../../source/guides/formats/index.md:1
msgid "Formats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/index.md:3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A **format** is the recipe for one report layout: `EURIZON-EN23`, "
"`AMUNDI-IT24`. Its name carries the issuer, the language and the "
"**earliest** year of the reports it reads. Layouts drift over the years, "
"so a later report from the same issuer often needs a format of its own; "
"when it does not, the existing format reads it and keeps its name — names"
" follow recipes, not documents ({doc}`../../reference/formats/names`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/index.md:9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Formats do not live in the engine. They live in a **formats repository**,"
" and this area is about what you put in one and how you work on it. Why "
"they live outside is {doc}`../../reference/design/formats-as-plugins`."
msgstr ""

